OL,3,AKenya confirms second Ebola case as
OL,4,Arelative of country's first victim
OL,5,
OL,6,FKenya has confirmed a second case of
OL,7,FEbola, 10 days after a businessman died
OL,8,Fof the virus after he had travelled to
OL,9,Fthe East African nation from the
OL,10,FDemocratic Republic of Congo.
OL,12,FThe new patient, a 39-year-old man, is
OL,13,Fa close relative of the first case and
OL,14,Fwas already in quarantine when he fell
OL,15,Fill on Tuesday, Kenya's health ministry
OL,16,Fsaid.
OL,18,FThe incubation period for Ebola ranges
OL,19,Ffrom two to 21 days, meaning those
OL,20,Fexposed to the virus may not become ill
OL,21,Ffor several weeks.
OL,23,APub: 14-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB Nat NewsC Nat TVF Clean Feed
